{literal}# Cookie Policy

Last updated: [UPDATE DATE]

## 1. What are cookies?

Cookies are small text files stored on your device (computer, phone,
tablet) when you use our online store [STORE NAME]. They let us recognize
your browser on your next visit and remember your preferences.

## 2. What cookies do we use?

### 2.1. Necessary cookies
Required for the basic operation of the store — e.g. keeping your
logged-in session, cart contents, and remembering your cookie decision.
They cannot be disabled, because the store would not work properly
without them.

### 2.2. Functional cookies
Remember your preferences (e.g. selected language, recently viewed
products). Disabling them won't break the store, but you'll lose some
convenience.

### 2.3. Analytics cookies
Help us understand how you use the store (e.g. Google Analytics) so we
can improve it. They do not contain data that personally identifies you.

### 2.4. Marketing cookies
Used to display personalized ads (e.g. Facebook Pixel, Google Ads) and to
measure the effectiveness of advertising campaigns.

## 3. How long do we keep cookies?

Each cookie has a defined lifetime — from the duration of a session
(deleted when you close the browser) up to a maximum of 24 months. A
detailed list of cookies and their retention times is available in the
"Cookie settings" panel in the footer of our website.

## 4. How to manage cookies?

You can change your preferences at any time:

- Click "Cookie settings" in the footer of our website.
- Or change the settings in your browser:
  - Chrome: https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647
  - Firefox: https://support.mozilla.org/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer
  - Safari: https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac
  - Edge: https://support.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge

## 5. Third-party cookies

Some cookies are set by our partners:

- Google LLC (Google Analytics, Google Ads)
- Meta Platforms, Inc. (Facebook Pixel)
- Hotjar Ltd (user behavior analysis)

Each of these parties has its own privacy policy describing how they
process data.

## 6. Your rights

Under the GDPR you have the right to:

- withdraw consent at any time,
- access your data,
- rectify your data,
- erase your data,
- restrict processing,
- data portability,
- object to processing,
- lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority.

